<h2>Hypothesis</h2>
<p>
  Mutation is the only source of novelty in the soup: nothing else writes bytes a program
  did not already contain. DESIGN §1.3 sweep 1 predicts a window. At
  <span class="mono">mutation_rate = 0</span> the soup can only shuffle what randomness
  handed it, so emergence is delayed; far above the error threshold — Eigen's
  quasispecies bound — a replicator's copies are corrupted faster than it can make them,
  and nothing persists. Between the two there should be a band of rates where the time to
  emergence is shortest.
</p>

<h2>Method</h2>
<p>
  A 128×128 torus of 64-byte tapes, 20 000 epochs per run, ten mutation rates from
  <span class="mono">0</span> up to <span class="mono">2<sup>-8</sup></span>, ten seeds
  each. Every other parameter is at its default. The dependent variable is
  <em>transition epoch</em> as defined in DESIGN §1.2: the first sampled epoch at which
  <span class="mono">compress_ratio</span> falls below 0.6 and stays below it for the next
  three samples. A run that never crosses that line is censored, not zero, and appears as
  a hollow marker along the top of the phase diagram.
</p>

<h2>Result (interim)</h2>
<p>
  Partial, and not yet a result. The numbers below cover the finished runs only, all of
  them 128×128 over 20 000 epochs.
</p>
<p>
  <strong>No transition in the low arms.</strong> At
  <span class="mono">mutation_rate = 0</span>, <span class="mono">2<sup>-16</sup></span>,
  <span class="mono">2<sup>-15</sup></span> and <span class="mono">2<sup>-14</sup></span>
  the count is 0 of 10 transitions in each arm, seeds 1 to 10. Those worlds end where they
  started: <span class="mono">compress_ratio</span> median 0.91 to 0.93 at 20 000 epochs
  and <span class="mono">replicator_count</span> 0.
</p>
<p>
  <strong>One transition at 2<sup>-13</sup>,</strong> 1 of 9 finished runs — run 41, seed
  1. Its <span class="mono">compress_ratio</span> sits at 0.94 until about epoch 5000,
  then falls 0.725 → 0.526 → 0.052 within 100 epochs and ends at 0.26 at 20 000 epochs;
  <span class="mono">entropy_bits</span> drops from 7.9 to 6.2 across the same window.
  <span class="mono">replicator_count</span> is 538 at epoch 5000 and peaks at 867, then
  is back to 0 after epoch 5500. The event is diverse rather than a single winner:
  <span class="mono">top_share</span> stays at or below 0.008 and
  <span class="mono">distinct_tapes</span> reaches 13 349. Run 45 (seed 5, same arm) is
  still running with a peak <span class="mono">replicator_count</span> of 108.
</p>
<p>
  <strong>Higher rates are unfinished.</strong> 0 of 4 finished runs have transitioned at
  <span class="mono">2<sup>-12</sup></span> so far, and the arms above it —
  <span class="mono">2<sup>-11</sup></span>, <span class="mono">2<sup>-10</sup></span>,
  <span class="mono">2<sup>-9</sup></span> and <span class="mono">2<sup>-8</sup></span> —
  contribute no finished run to this tally.
</p>
<p>
  This section is held until the high arms and run 45 finish, and even then it is not
  readable as a negative result: the <span class="mono">bff-control</span> positive
  control has not transitioned yet, so a flat sweep would say nothing about the
  hypothesis. One discrepancy is under investigation: the
  <span class="mono">transition_epoch</span> recorded for run 41 is 9900, while its own
  samples first fall below 0.6 at epoch 5030.
</p>
